  "notes": "Cash basis county; governmental funds only. Receipts/disbursements from Total Governmental Funds column of the Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (p4). Beginning cash = beginning fund balance as adjusted 20,810,186 (p4); ending 17,773,365 = cash 5,208,568 + investments 7,576,970 + restricted cash 4,987,827 (p3). Taxes 18,120,569 split by statement of activities general receipts (p2): property 15,204,208, motor vehicle 1,649,757, lodging 1,258,654, other 7,950 (sum matches). Local receipts 4,398,669 not broken down on p4 (p2 charges/interest/miscellaneous do not add to it, so no split), category charges for services/fees (dominant part per p2 statement of activities) with review. Intergovernmental 9,256,813 is printed only as a broad group (no homestead/credit/pro-rate breakdown in the trimmed PDF). Transfers in/out each 4,259,443 net to zero. Balance sheet (attempt 2) from the governmental funds Statement of Assets and Fund Balances - Cash Basis (p3, Total Governmental Funds column), whose totals equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1, 17,773,365); fund balance by classification (restricted, committed, unassigned). No liabilities. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p6) used for General Fund (more detailed than combining p5, not double counted); its function groups are by department so they differ from p4 function totals (capital outlay is embedded in lines). Inheritance Tax Fund taken from p5 combining statement; General Fund column on p5 plus inheritance = total General Fund. Road, Highway Buyback, Courthouse schedules print disbursements as one line. Courthouse Building single disbursements line 107,980 (p9) is category capital outlay, the dominant part per the p4 fund column (capital outlay 96,010 + general government 11,970; attempt 3 fix 2026-10-28). Other nonmajor funds have no schedule in the trimmed PDF. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
